, ["Can", 284.6], ["you", 284.66], ["move", 284.78], ["a", 285.0], ["little?", 285.14]], [["A", 286.57], ["big", 286.57], ["truck", 286.76], ["was", 287.04], ["blocking", 287.36], ["the", 287.82], ["road.", 288.0]]]}}, {"n": 14, "w": "satisfy", "pos": "v.", "zh": "满足（需要、欲望）", "ex": "To satisfy means to give someone what they need or want, so they feel it is enough. You satisfy your hunger when you eat.", "exs": ["Nothing seems to satisfy him. He always wants more.", "This salad won't satisfy me. I need real food."], "t": 289.36, "src": {"t": "So two paths to happiness: one path is success, you get what you want, you satisfy your material needs,", "a": "audio/t01/s11.mp3", "hl": [75, 82], "sp": "Naval", "oa": "audio/t01o/s11.mp3", "oab": [5.58, 6.86]}, "tt": {"w": 289.36, "ex": [["To", 292.55], ["satisfy", 292.72], ["means", 292.78], ["to", 293.26], ["give", 293.54], ["someone", 293.7], ["what", 294.02], ["they", 294.32], ["need", 294.5], ["or", 294.8], ["want,", 295.1], ["so", 295.76], ["they", 296.08], ["feel", 296.22], ["it", 296.46], ["is", 296.72], ["enough.", 296.84], ["You", 297.86], ["satisfy", 297.92], ["your", 298.22], ["hunger", 298.76], ["when", 299.08], ["you", 299.34], ["eat.", 299.48]], "exs": [[["Nothing", 302.91], ["seems", 303.04], ["to", 303.3], ["satisfy", 303.58], ["him.", 303.9], ["He", 304.84], ["always", 305.0], ["wants", 305.18], ["more.", 305.66]], [["This", 307.3], ["salad", 307.3], ["won't", 307.6], ["satisfy", 307.98], ["me.", 308.28], ["I", 309.3], ["need", 309.36], ["real", 309.56], ["food.", 309.82]]]}}, {"n": 15, "w": "material needs", "pos": "n. phrase", "zh": "物质需求", "ex": "Material needs are the things you need for your body and daily life, like food, a home, clothes and money. They are things, not feelings.", "exs": ["Once your material needs are met, money matters less.", "Work can meet your material needs, but not all your needs."], "t": 311.57, "src": {"t": "So two paths to happiness: one path is success, you get what you want,